## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design a production-ready online continual learning system under delayed feedback, latency, memory limits, and non-stationary user behavior, with fairness concerns.

## Key Concepts

- Online continual learning with delayed labels
- Factorization machines and warm-start online SGD
- Calibration, drift detection, and memory-budget governance

## Code Example

```javascript
// Skeleton online update loop for streaming features
function onlineUpdate(x, y, w, lr) {
  const pred = 1 / (1 + Math.exp(-dot(w, x)));
  const g = pred - y;
  for (let i = 0; i < x.length; i++) w[i] -= lr * g * x[i];
  return w;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you monitor for calibration drift in production?
- How would you enforce fairness constraints without sacrificing overall performance?

## Why This Is Asked
In production, data distributions shift during events; online adaptation with tight latency is essential for edge-scale detectors. This tests practical drift handling and monitoring under real constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Online learning with bounded memory
- Concept drift detection (ADWIN, EDDM)
- Catastrophic forgetting mitigation (replay buffers, ensembles)
- Online calibration (isotonic regression, Platt scaling)
- Streaming infra and latency targets

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: online drift detector usage
let detector = new ADWIN(0.002);
let model = new OnlineModel();
function onInstance(x, y){
  let pred = model.predict(x);
  detector.update(Math.abs(pred - y));
  if (detector.driftDetected()){
     model.updateWithReplayBuffer();
  }
  model.partialFit(x, y);
}
```

