## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses understanding of privacy-preserving, real-time ML systems that operate across devices and cloud infrastructure. It tests knowledge of multimodal processing, latency optimization, federated learning, and production ML lifecycle management.

## Key Concepts
- On-device inference with early-exit classifiers for sub-60ms latency
- Server-side multimodal fusion for ambiguous cases
- Federated learning with secure aggregation for privacy-preserving model updates
- Latency budgeting across device tiers and cloud GPUs
- Drift detection and model calibration
- Language-agnostic feature extraction

## Code Example
```javascript
// On-device early-exit classifier skeleton
async function moderateContent(input) {
  const preprocessed = await preprocess(input);
  const earlyExit = await runEarlyExitModel(preprocessed);

  if (earlyExit.confidence > 0.95) {
    return { decision: earlyExit.label, source: 'on-device' };
  }
  if (earlyExit.confidence > 0.7) {
    const encrypted = await encryptForServer(preprocessed);
    const serverResult = await sendToFusionModel(encrypted);
    return { decision: serverResult.label, source: 'server' };
  }
  return { decision: 'review', source: 'manual' };
}
```

